/// Initiates a point-in-time recovery of a user pool to a time in the past
/// that you specify. This operation is the first step of a recovery and
/// doesn't change your user pool data. Amazon Cognito pauses write
/// operations in the user pool and generates a recovery preview, which
/// might not be available immediately. The preview shows the number of
/// entities that the recovery creates, updates, and deletes. To check the
/// status of the recovery and review the preview, make a request. When the
/// status is PREVIEW_GENERATED , apply the recovery with a request or
/// discard it with a request. The time that it takes to generate the
/// recovery preview doesn't depend on the size of your user pool.
/// Point-in-time recovery is a disaster recovery feature. Use it to recover
/// from accidental or unauthorized changes that affect your user data, for
/// example the deletion or corruption of many users. Don't use
/// point-in-time recovery to remove users that were created recently or to
/// revert changes to individual users. To delete or update individual
